coder › Done on branch `feat/done-command` (3 commits).

What changed:
- `src/store.ts`: added `markDone(todos, id)` — returns a new array via `map`/spread with that todo `done: true`, throws `RangeError("no todo with id <id>")` when missing, never mutates input. Changed `render` to `"<id>. [x] <text>"` for done and `"<id>. [ ] <text>"` otherwise.
- `src/cli.ts`: added `done <id>` — parses with `Number` + `Number.isInteger`, calls `markDone`, prints `done: <text>\n` code 0; on non-whole-number or unknown id prints `error: no todo with id <id>\n` code 1 with `todos` unchanged.
- Tests: new `src/store.test.ts` (no-mutate + `RangeError` naming id); extended `src/cli.test.ts` (done success + `[x]`/`[ ]` list output, unknown-id error, non-whole-number `abc`/`1.5` errors, todos unchanged).

Decisions not in the spec:
- `done` with missing/empty id is treated as invalid (`error: no todo with id <raw>`, code 1) — this also avoids `Number('') === 0` matching id 0.
- Invalid-format errors echo the raw string (`abc`, `1.5`); unknown-id errors echo the normalized number (`Number(raw)`), matching `markDone`'s message. `catch` in the CLI just reformats any `markDone` throw into the `error:` line.
- Left the `usage:` line untouched (smallest change).

